    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Suppose log10 5 = a/b [B1] with positive integers a, b. [A1] Exponentiate to base ten: 10log10 5 = 10a/b, hence 5 = 10a/b. Raising both sides to the power b gives 5b = (10a/b)b. Then 10a = 5b. [A1] Every positive power of 5 ends in 5 (for example 5, 25, 125, 625), whereas every positive power of 10 ends in 0. The left side is even and the right side is odd, a contradiction: [A1] Thus log10 5 is irrational . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:657.3px\"></figure>",
