      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"For A̸ = 0, cancel A: 15r2 −5r = 12r2 −2 3r2 −5r + 2 = 0 (3r −2)(r −1) = 0 This gives r = 2/3 or r = 1. Equivalently, the geometric terms a + 6d, a + 3d, a + d give (a + 3d)2 = (a + 6d)(a + d), d(3d −a) = 0. [M1] [A1] For d = 0, the defined ratio is 1. [A1] For d̸ = 0, a = 3d [A1] and the ratio is 6d/(9d) = 2/3. [A1] The possible values are 1, 2/3 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 9 marks.</p>"
