    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The vertices of the triangle  OAB have coordinates A ( 6, 18, 6 − − ) , ( B 7, 1,3 − ) , where O is a fixed origin. The point N lies on OA so that ON : NA = 1: 2 . The point M is the midpoint of OB . The point P is the intersection of AM and BN . By using vector methods, or otherwise, determine the coordinates of P . ( 10 )\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
