      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"and b = −−→ OB. [A1] Then −−→ ON = a/3 [A1] and −−→ OM = b/2. [A1] The source writes −−→ NP = k−−→ NB, with 0 &lt; k &lt; 1. As N = (2, −6, −2) and M = (7/2, −1/2, 3/2), B −N = (5, 5, 5), giving −−→ NP = (5k, 5k, 5k). Following the two paths gives −−→ MP = −m + n + −−→ NP = (5k −3/2, 5k −11/2, 5k −7/2), −→ PA = −−−→ NP + 2n = (4 −5k, −12 −5k, −4 −5k).\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q12-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Since these vectors are parallel, set −−→ MP = λ−→ PA. The first two components give 5k −3 2 = −5λk + 4λ 5k −11 2 = −5λk −12λ 4λ + 3 2 = 11 2 −12λ 16λ = 4 λ = 1 4 5k −3 2 = −5 4k + 1 25 4 k = 5 2 k = 2 5\" style=\"--madas-width:414.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q12-solution-4.svg\" alt=\"The third components agree: 2 −7/2 = −3/2 = (1/4)(−2 −4). Thus P = N + (2, 2, 2) = (4, −4, 0).\" style=\"--madas-width:420.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-s/q12-solution-5.svg\" alt=\"Equivalently, on AM the position vector of P is (1 −s)a + (s/2)b, and on NB it is ((1 −t)/3)a + tb. [A1] Matching the coefficients gives s/2 = t [A1] = 2/5 and 1 −s = 1/5. [A1] Hence P = 1 5(6, −18, −6) + 2 5(7, −1, 3) = (4, −4, 0) . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
